WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.879
Five identical notes, all reading "Are you
sentient?"

00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:07.420
were written and copied by Dr. Veritas in
preparation for the experiment.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:11.400
A note was placed on the setting "Fine," and
produced a note containing an excerpt from

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.830
the 1641 treatise 'Meditation on First Philosophy’
by René Descartes in Latin.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:23.380
It read: 'I am, I exist, whenever it is uttered
from me, or conceived by the mind, necessarily

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.380
is true.'

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.350
The next note was placed inside on the setting
"Very Fine."

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:31.890
What emerged was an excerpt from the essay
'An Essay Concerning Human Understanding'

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:37.350
by Philosopher John Locke reading: 'This Source
of Ideas, every Man has wholly in himself

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:42.399
… And though it be not Sense, as having
nothing to do with external Objects; yet it

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:46.690
is very like it, and might properly enough
be called internal Sense.'

